  "description": "The NZ Loyal Party is a far-right party. Founded in 2023 by antivax activist Liz Gunn, the party’s program revolves around opposition to ‘globalist’ institutions such as the United Nations, Banks, and the World Economic Forum. It opposes both immigration and taxation. The party is currently led by far-right activist Kelvyn Alp. He has a background in conspiracy media, an armed militia that has targeted bankers, and has been involved in legal battles regarding the distribution of videos from the Christchurch Mosque attacks. It has never won a seat in parliament.",
